    "updated_at": "2018-04-20T20:57:38Z",
    "body": "No worries. I guess it looks like in most cases the callers are already OK: for example, \r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/window-object.html#closing-browsing-contexts:unload-a-document says \"Unload X, with the recycle parameter set to Y\", which seems about right. (Arguably \"Unload a document passing X and Y\" would be more uniform, but it's a bit harder to read, so I'm fine to leave it as-is.)\r\n\r\nGoing through all the callers of \"unload a document\" at least, they seem to be fine. I think that part of my bulleted list is not really actionable. So, good question!",
